#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124437 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124241 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "049e8586-8348-50be-ac56-4ea79eba43cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Slope of the Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"}] :question/id #uuid "225b0bca-3520-58ab-bd36-0e3de337b604" :question/math-academy-id "e-3068" :question/problem "A surface $S$ is defined by $z=f(x,y).$ The curve $C$ is the intersection of $S$ with the plane $x=2.$ Given that the point $P(2,1,8)$ lies on $C,$ and that $f_y = \\dfrac{4x}y - 4x^2y,$ find the slope of the tangent to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=2.$ So, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P(2,1,8)$ will be given by the partial derivative $f_y(2,1).$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $f_y(x,y)$ at $(2,1)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(2,1) & =\\frac{4(2)}{(1)}-4(2)^{2}(1) \\\\  & =8-16 \\\\  & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "049e8586-8348-50be-ac56-4ea79eba43cd" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048707}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531801 :question-generator/id #uuid "06977e38-001b-5371-84fb-705d2090e87e" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186124437.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124957 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "049e8586-8348-50be-ac56-4ea79eba43cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Slope of the Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bf0df7e-022b-5418-9924-365a7162eff3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321611} {:answer/id #uuid "3fa3c59a-6624-5598-a1a5-f291f19779f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321648