ed}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335768 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "049e8586-8348-50be-ac56-4ea79eba43cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Slope of the Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c9a56e0-5972-5209-9d5c-ea16e82e995f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333100} {:answer/id #uuid "66686a01-21cc-56d7-951a-bacb93258c0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333921} {:answer/id #uuid "79013707-fe29-522d-ac8d-ac18b46d1880" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334075} {:answer/id #uuid "989e0c9d-3b24-5671-9e42-b86c26764caf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334342} {:answer/id #uuid "b3886518-c45d-5987-8dfe-39a52ed04936" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66686a01-21cc-56d7-951a-bacb93258c0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333921} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a4e3654-a019-5e30-92b9-ed3bae770d8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335446}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1f6c71da-f5b0-5c03-871d-e07fb324730c" :question/math-academy-id "q-64968" :question/problem "A surface $S$ is defined by $z=f(x,y).$ The curve $C$ is the intersection of $S$ with the plane $x=1.$ Given that the point $P$ with $y$-coordinate $0$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=\\sqrt{2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy+\\frac{\\pi }{4})$, find the slope of the tangent to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point where $y=0$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(1,0).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(1,0):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,0) & =\\sqrt{2}(1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\cdot 0+\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338912 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "049e8586-8348-50be-ac56-4ea79eba43cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Slope of the Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34d5f7cf-613e-525d-93c2-0c7080720d91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336530} {:answer/id #uuid "6b07d985-3564-5d0a-b070-9e5e048515e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336980} {:answer/id #uuid "c6298338-e8f0-5052-8bae-ef3ddf73ce7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337789} {:answer/id #uuid "e6ad9eb0-f197-5640-819b-488c340e4e28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338046} {:answer/id #uuid "f52f84db-f262-57d1-9c5e-5a630266362b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6ad9eb0-f197-5640-819b-488c340e4e28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338046} :answer-field/id #uuid "7598b8df-f496-507a-9973-2189f2324d0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6efe9457-81ed-5961-99c6-f2de702a7e78" :question/math-academy-id "q-71198" :question/problem "A surface $S$ is defined by $z=f(x,y).$ The curve $C$ is the intersection of $S$ with the plane $x=2.$ Given that the point $P$ with $y$-coordinate $1$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=3{x}^{2}y-6x{y}^{2}$, find the slope of the tangent to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point where $y=1$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(2,1).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(2,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(2,1) & =3(2)^{2}(1)-6(2)(1)^{2} \\\\  & =12-12 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383293 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "049e8586-8348-50be-ac56-4ea79eba43cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Slope of the Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4997e6e-db2a-59f0-8089-3716fd8ae7ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383295} {:answer/id #uuid "e6b94256-12a4-5e4a-a7be-2faa95e83174" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383296} {:answer/id #uuid "aa5682d4-84d4-5541-90d8-7e7040c8235e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383297} {:answer/id #uuid "1592e766-be1b-5bdf-ac2c-4264db8109b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383298} {:answer/id #uuid "749b8f4c-62f7-5c59-bc47-3128b8a6da53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa5682d4-84d4-5541-90d8-7e7040c8235e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383297} :answer-field/id #uuid "24582cee-9319-59e6-9a06-ddc0dc01268c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-fie