rivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ at $(0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(0,1) & ={2}^{0+1}(1)(0\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+1)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436951 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "049e8586-8348-50be-ac56-4ea79eba43cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Slope of the Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e1e7001-fa28-52e7-9159-e1a9952ad01c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436941} {:answer/id #uuid "5212a9fa-3e07-5070-b235-7a3b34cb5bd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436943} {:answer/id #uuid "7ba5571e-63b9-59ee-98ea-36a27b8aac00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436944} {:answer/id #uuid "cc662000-df0c-5f2c-a156-05cd36f47ab9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436948} {:answer/id #uuid "e1a14c70-f4ee-5c8e-bd4a-ccddfe87a87e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5212a9fa-3e07-5070-b235-7a3b34cb5bd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436943} :answer-field/id #uuid "aee200cc-d9b2-5d5b-a23a-38088da4f688" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436950}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0063a739-db3e-5983-b65e-bb4c57fabf9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-64967" :question/problem "A surface $S$ is defined by $z=f(x,y).$ The curve $C$ is the intersection of $S$ with the plane $y=1.$ Given that the point $P$ with $x$-coordinate $\\pi $ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=y{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$, find the slope of the tangent to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point where $x=\\pi $ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(\\pi ,1).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ at $(\\pi ,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(\\pi ,1) & =(1){e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1) \\\\  & ={e}^{0}(-1) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531731 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "049e8586-8348-50be-ac56-4ea79eba43cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Slope of the Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65e5c3f0-5773-5bbd-a23a-3a43d1fc086e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531761} {:answer/id #uuid "6b202fc5-7a82-5091-9da5-936069a8528b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{727}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531763} {:answer/id #uuid "9e2a14ab-0cce-5725-9c80-5f9d2f8d0921" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "182" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531782} {:answer/id #uuid "bf400e9b-bb0b-5054-8ef9-7e5f7d9ae05b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "197" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531789} {:answer/id #uuid "f958d464-4ab0-5f12-8833-fb278b8eb146" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{713}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f958d464-4ab0-5f12-8833-fb278b8eb146" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{713}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531799} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c8c9430-d63b-5c40-bd47-a82c98a21776" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531746}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db